          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "すいか (suika) is Sino-Japanese, borrowed from Chinese, \"western melon\": sui, \"west\", and ka, \"melon\" (Middle Chinese kwae). Sui is a later Chinese reading of the character for west, not the usual sei (JMdict; Unihan, KANJIDIC2)."
